Well there is a quick and DIRTY way. Put all the new RPMS (which you
want to upgrade) in one directory and do a rpm -Uhv --nodeps  --force
*.rpm (I had to do it twice and I replaced rpm as the last thing), et
voilà you are running rh 5.2. If anything does not install just
reinstall it after everything else is processed. I did this from 5.0 to
5.1 and from 5.1 to 5.2. But beware as I have to take down my jensen on
a regular basis to switch to another OS I have no idea whether this is
suitable for HA-systems.
